    {
      "name": "WebSocket (Socket.IO)",
      "description": "Socket.IO connections cannot be included in a standard Postman collection.\nCreate a new Socket.IO request manually in Postman (New → Socket.IO).\n\nNamespace: /polls\nURL: http://localhost:3000/polls\n\nEvents to emit (client → server):\n  • joinPoll   payload: <pollId: number>   — subscribe to poll room, receives current results immediately\n  • leavePoll  payload: <pollId: number>   — unsubscribe from poll room\n\nEvents to listen (server → client):\n  • resultsUpdated  payload: { pollId, title, questions: [{ questionId, text, options: [{ optionId, text, votes }] }] }\n\nQuick test with Node.js:\n  const { io } = require('socket.io-client');\n  const socket = io('http://localhost:3000/polls');\n  socket.emit('joinPoll', 1);\n  socket.on('resultsUpdated', console.log);",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "⚠ Socket.IO — read description above",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{host}}/polls",
              "host": ["{{host}}"],
              "path": ["polls"]
            },
            "description": "This is a placeholder. Socket.IO connections must be created manually:\n1. In Postman click New → Socket.IO\n2. Set URL to: http://localhost:3000/polls\n3. Connect, then emit 'joinPoll' with body: 1\n4. Listen for 'resultsUpdated' event\n\nOr test via Node.js:\nconst { io } = require('socket.io-client');\nconst socket = io('http://localhost:3000/polls');\nsocket.emit('joinPoll', 1);\nsocket.on('resultsUpdated', (data) => console.log(JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)));"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
